================================================================================
Mermaid
================================================================================
https://mermaid.js.org/
Version: 10.9.5
Files: mermaid.min.txt

Mermaid's own code is MIT. The file is its whole dependency tree compiled into one
bundle, so other projects' code travels inside it. Everything in there is MIT except
DOMPurify:

    DOMPurify 3.2.4          MPL-2.0 or Apache-2.0. See the section below.
    js-yaml 4.1.0            MIT, in a banner in the file.
    A Promises/A+ 1.1.1      MIT, in a banner, copyright Ralf S. Engelschall.
      thenable
    An event object based    MIT, in a banner naming jQuery's license.
      on jQuery's events
    A Bezier curve           MIT, in a banner, copyright Gaetan Renaudeau.
      generator
    A Runge-Kutta spring     MIT, in a banner, adapted from Framer.js, copyright
      generator                Koen Bok.
    KaTeX 0.16.11            MIT, and the KaTeX text above is that license. A second
                             copy of KaTeX, later than the 0.16.9 files above. It
                             carries no banner, so the license is upstream's, and the
                             version string is in the bundle.
    cytoscape.js, with       MIT per upstream, github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape.js and
      its cose-bilkent         github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape.js-cose-bilkent.
      layout                   Neither states a license or a version in this build.

Reading those for yourself: every banner, then the two versions that are only in a
string. The tr joins the file's few line breaks so that a banner written over several
lines still prints as one. Two of the eight banners it finds are comments of Mermaid's
own, "Check if previously processed" and "Wait for document loaded", and carry no
license; the other six are the notices listed above.

    tr '\n' ' ' < mermaid.min.txt | grep -o '/\*!.\{0,160\}'
    grep -o 'version:"0\.16\.[0-9]*"' mermaid.min.txt
    grep -o 'Mje="10\.9\.[0-9]*"' mermaid.min.txt

