================================================================================
DOMPurify
================================================================================
https://github.com/cure53/DOMPurify
Version: 3.2.4
Bundled inside: mermaid.min.txt

Copyright 2025 Dr.-Ing. Mario Heiderich, Cure53 and other contributors

DOMPurify is dual-licensed. It may be used under EITHER the Mozilla Public
License, Version 2.0, OR the Apache License, Version 2.0. Satisfying one is
enough; you do not have to satisfy both. The upstream package declares this as:

    "license": "(MPL-2.0 OR Apache-2.0)"

Both licenses permit redistribution. Apache-2.0 is permissive; MPL-2.0 is
copyleft at file level, reaching only the file DOMPurify is compiled into.

The full text of each is in a file of its own next to this one, unmodified:

    LICENSE-APACHE-2.0.txt
      Taken from https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cure53/DOMPurify/3.4.11/LICENSE
      which is byte for byte the text published at
      https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.txt
      SHA-256 cfc7749b96f63bd31c3c42b5c471bf756814053e847c10f3eb003417bc523d30

    LICENSE-MPL-2.0.txt
      Taken from https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cure53/DOMPurify/3.4.11/LICENSE-MPL
      SHA-256 fab3dd6bdab226f1c08630b1dd917e11fcb4ec5e1e020e2c16f83a0a13863e85

Neither file has a header added to it, because a license reproduced inexactly is
not the license. The MPL text is taken from DOMPurify rather than from
mozilla.org because the two differ in two characters: what mozilla.org currently
serves at /media/MPL/2.0/index.txt has dropped a trailing space on one line and
changed the scheme in the Exhibit A URL from http to https.

The two texts are the ones DOMPurify ships as separate files at tag 3.4.11. At
tag 3.2.4, the version bundled here, DOMPurify shipped the same dual grant in a
single LICENSE file: a preamble naming the choice, then both texts in full. The
grant is identical either way, and taking the texts from 3.4.11 keeps one copy
of each in the pack rather than two near-identical ones.

Confirming the version yourself:

    grep -o '@license DOMPurify [0-9.]*' mermaid.min.txt
